<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chlodio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 430–450</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chlodio was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a> in the first half of the 5th century, mentioned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a>. Around the 440s he advanced into Roman territory, took Cambrai and occupied the land as far as the Somme, despite a defeat by the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> at Vicus Helena. Later tradition counted him among the ancestors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty">Merovingian dynasty</a>.</p></div>
